knowledge-base/reference/canonical-data-map.html:6225:      "description": "One take-off and one landing, with its schedule, estimates and actual times.",
knowledge-base/reference/canonical-data-map.html:8784:        "lifecycle": "pending → emitted → retracted, or pending → unlandable{reason}: out_of_population, out_of_window, refused, subject_pending (the crew has no base), deleted_before_landing (→ retracted). An item still pending after T_land (tenants/\u003cid>/sync.json sickCall.landWithinSeconds, default 300) is unlandable{timeout}. unlandable is critical (absence_report_unlandable): a sick call the platform could not route, for the operator to handle by hand. Items carry subject_id (a CHECK requires it, §6.7), so erasure deletes them (no erased state: a deleted item has no state; dba 0.10 info); an emitted item is kept while its sick-call task is open (the router and the reconcile resolve through it), then expires with the window.",
knowledge-base/reference/canonical-data-map.html:13618:        "FlightLeg.operationalDate: the 'ADATE semantics open' note closed. The habit of reading ADATE as the landing day is NOT confirmed — it is refuted on 2,666 of 16,000 legs"
knowledge-base/reference/canonical-data-map.html:13975:      "question": "Is landing currency an EXPI kind ('90 Day' in the legacy seed, review §7)?",
knowledge-base/reference/canonical-data-map.html:17224:        "item": "sick call after landing: the absence_report lifecycle, the line key on the log port, the router's resolver, the bridge parked not thrown, the reset cursor carried",
knowledge-base/reference/canonical-data-map.html:17448:      "finding": "the land timeout equals the pending alert's threshold; a line landing after it is never routed; the unlandable page clears itself (an any-increase rule), so it needs an acknowledged gauge; a reset truncates the only record of an unlandable sick call (contract: reset refuses with CE003, §10.3); the consumer's and the sweeper's host and cadence are unstated; a re-entered sick call collides on the item key",
knowledge-base/reference/canonical-data-map.html:17619:<script type="application/json" id="derived-data">{"current":["Airport","CrewMember","CrewCurrency","DocumentExpiry","FlightLeg","FlightAlert","FlightMemo","FlightDisruptionState","PaxImpactRecord","CrewDutySegment","CrewCheckIn","CrewLegAssignment","CrRouteAssignment","DutyPeriod","Absence","ReserveBlock","VacationBlock","Pairing","ConnectionLeg","OpenTime","CrewRequest","CoverageDemand","FdpExtension","NearbyStationPresence","CrewAlert"],"proposed":["Qualification","CrewGroupMembership","CrewGroup","CrewDocument","DocumentType","CrewMember","ContactPoint","Address","CrewBaseAssignment","CrewNote","ChangeEvent","RosterActivity","DutyPeriod","Pairing","PairingSegment","FlightLeg","FlightDelay","EntryRequirement","CrewComplementRequirement","Airport","Country","Carrier","Aircraft","AircraftType","CrewPosition","CodeListEntry"],"changes":{"rosterDiffs":[["Absence event lifecycle (crew.absence_reported / _retracted from LOG_ROSTER)","Absence entity","Behaviour of RosterActivity lines with category = absence; natural key and payload unchanged"],["Sick-call demand source (affectedFlightLegRefs, written by a later enrichment)","Absence","absence.affectedFlightLegRefs"],["Classification (unplanned, fatigueRelated, healthRelated: sensitive)","Absence","absence.classification.*, leaf-tagged; RosterActivity becomes class C (still sealed under the crew key)"],["Reserve class and ReserveClassConfig (cascade, windows, fairness) used by Forge prep","ReserveBlock","reserve.classCode + reserve.classConfigRef; the contactable window stays computed by Forge (CR003-E6, not overturned)"],["Reserve rostered position (callout gate)","ReserveBlock upsert only","The line's positionCode"],["Vacation floor-reduction meaning and month-wide refresh window","VacationBlock and its own refresh","leave.classConfigRef → tenant leave classes; the roster read window for category = leave"],["Population scope: absence ignores crew bases, reserve and vacation scope by base","Three reads","One read with a per-category population predicate"]],"mergeReasons":[["One source fact, already one read.","All three are ROSTER rows with a negative LEG_FLT code (82,389 of 175,648 rows in the operated window); the adapter already reads them with one generic SQL under three keys; N-OC models every line as a RosterActivity. Keeping them apart needed a router, a refusal state and a critical alert whose only job was to defend the split."],["Every protection the split bought survives.","healthRelated exists only under absence.classification, so non-absence lines have nothing to scrub; reserve authority is one closed enum value validated at write; reserve and leave are distinct enum values with a read-plane test pinning the filter; DutyPeriod still excludes absence and reserve, so the CR003-D1 blocker is not reintroduced."],["It removes defects and gains capabilities.","Completeness is one query instead of a four-entity union; airport standby can attach to a DutyPeriod; absence lines gain the rostered position; the fabricated occurredAt of crew.absence_reported becomes the log row's own time (absence.reportedAt); one day definition (base-local dutyDate)."]],"catalogue":[["Carrier","AIMS CARRIERS (ID, CODE); N-OC AirlineCode / ICAOAirlineCode","tenant subsidiary.carriers {designator, relationship own | affiliate | partner, inOperatingScope}, keyed by designator"],["AircraftType","AIMS vvAIRCTYPE (26 rows); N-OC GetAircrafts distinct Type","qualification-family rule (Control Tower) and freighter/scope exclusion (tenant config), keyed by type code"],["CrewPosition","AIMS vvPositions (CODE, DESC_, CK_CB, RANK, ALTRN); N-OC Ranks","tenant positionConfigs (group, floatOrder, labels, isCommand) keyed by position code; canOperateAs in rule data"],["CodeListEntry","AIMS vvALERTYPE, vvFlightMemoCateg, DLYCD, CREWCAT, distinct LEGMAIN.CNXREASON / FLTYPE, PHONE_n_COMKIND; N-OC REASON","per scheme, the tenant config the referencing field's …ConfigRef names"],["CrewGroup (a scheme of CodeListEntry)","AIMS CREWCAT (240 rows; label only)","carrier (78 = CM, 79 = P5, 94 = Wingo), seniority list, special-airport category: tenant config"],["ActivityCode","AIMS vvCrewCodes (ID is the negative ROSTER.LEG_FLT marker); N-OC REFERENCE_ACTIVITY","tenant activity mapping (code → category, absence classification, reserve class, leave class) via RosterActivity.activityConfigRef"],["DocumentType","AIMS EXPI (SHORTDESC, DESC_, SEVERITY, MINDUE, MAXDUE, DAYTYP, EFFECTIVE_BEG/END)","Control Tower docrules: hasExpiry, grace, renewal lead, blocksDutyWhenInvalid, isTravelDocument, tier, action; keyed by the catalogue code"]],"newRulings":[["Six catalogue entity tables","Carrier, AircraftType, CrewPosition, CodeListEntry, ActivityCode, DocumentType. Amends ruling 17's entity set from 29 tables to 32 and reverses blueprint 0.5 §4.8's config / rule-data line for these names."],["R3 security ruling for roster_activity.category","One clear column (ruling 11 asks per entity and column), or the explicit choice of decrypt-and-filter reads (about 5,900 code lines a day at Copa, about 170 of them reserve, measured by P32). Ruled: the clear column (0.6-2)."],["RosterActivity subject class B → C","It now holds the sensitive absence.classification.healthRelated. No storage change: every crew-linked body is sealed under the crew key either way."],["dutyDate defined base-local","On RosterActivity and DutyPeriod. On AIMS this changes the date of a night duty relative to today's CrewDutySegment (the leg's UTC day); the legality differential must prove the verdicts before cutover. P27 showed AIMS has no per-duty day to copy (DUTYDAY is a pairing anchor), so the value is computed on AIMS whatever its zone."],["Pairing identity = the source ref","pairingNumber + startDate stay business fields and spine columns. P8 and P28: (CDATE, CROUTE) is the AIMS identity grammar; startDate is a UTC day (decision N1)."],["FlightLeg.estimated.source values renamed","aeroapi → external_feed; read planes that print the provenance change."],["CrewAlert.isLegalityType removed","Resolved per alert type through alertTypeConfigRef (7 non-test files)."],["DutyPeriod.pairingRef removed","New in 0.5, so no standing decision is overturned."],["Spine set re-opened again (open decision 9)","Spine columns on the six catalogue tables (codes, scheme, sourceCrewClass)."],["No stored positionConfigRef on position fields","Qualification, RosterActivity, OpenTime, CoverageDemand and others: the position policy key is the code (R13). Records what 0.5 did silently when it split CrewMember.positions."]],"stillOpen":"Ruled on 2026-10-02 (\"go with your recommendations on the rulings\"): the ten 0.6 overturns and the seven carried 0.5 decisions are listed under Rulings. Two are not final: 0.5-4 (sense_noc on the one-time reset) is deferred until the N-OC namespacing PR measures, and 0.5-8 (CrewNote) is stored but the security sign-off is still owed. The seven new decisions N1 to N7 that the probe results raised have recommendations and no ruling yet. Confirmed, not overturned: the operator instruction of 2026-09-19 that position groups stay tenant config.","fold":[["CrewCurrency now has an AIMS producer","Supersedes the adapter refusal (MssqlAimsDb.getCrewCurrency, domains/airline/crew/adapters/src/aims/mssqlDb.ts:1499-1515) and the \"no verified source\" KB section. The producer reads CREXPREC rows of the EXPI kinds the tenant configures as currency kinds (Copa: \"90 Day\", T/O + landing currency, 2,673 records, 1,616 current; \"90d E9\" has 4 records, 0 current). EXPIDATE becomes qualifiedUntil and CHKLAST becomes the new field lastQualifyingEventOn (a day, so not written into the instant lastEventAt). vvCREWDB.LASTACDAY_n is not a source (0 for every crew). A follow-up adapter change wires the read and the seeded alarms.","P25, P20; decision N2"],["ADATE is not read","LEGMAIN.ADATE is neither the arrival day nor a local date: the 2,666 of 16,000 legs that land on the next UTC day still carry ADATE = DAY, and it is never DAY + 1. FlightLeg.scheduled.arrival is DAY + STA (pre-wrapped) and FlightLeg.localDepartureDate is computed from scheduled.departure in the origin station's zone. No field is sourced from ADATE.","P11"],["Pairing.startDate and endDate are UTC days from CDATE","Their dateZone is redefined from base-local-day to utc-day: CDATE is the first leg's UTC day (delta 0 on 12,154 pairings in every departure hour, never negative) and ENDDATE is the last leg's UTC day (10,568 of 12,543 in the window). A base-local pairing day would be computed from the optional, inferred Pairing.base, and no regime counts pairing days; duty days keep the base-local rule.","P28, P16; decision N1"],["DutyPeriod.dutyDate is computed base-local","ROSTER.DUTYDAY is a pairing anchor, not a per-duty day: it is 2 to 13 days before LEG_DAY on at least 12,615 of 93,259 flight rows (13.5%). dutyDate is the base-local day of the duty's report, in the zone of the crew's base valid that day, and is never copied from DUTYDAY. Ruling 0.6-4 (base-local) stands and is now evidenced.","P27; ruling 0.6-4; decision N5"],["Birth and hire dates decode as yyyymmdd only","BIRTH and HIRE are not two formats: every ddmmyyyy-shaped value also matches yyyymmdd (yyyymmdd + empty = 9,347 on both columns). Accepting ddmmyyyy as well would mis-read real dates. An invalid value is the named state crew_date_undecodable (field absent, counted; measured volume 0).","P1"],["RosterActivity.category is the one sanctioned clear spine column on a crew table","An explicit R3 exception (ruling 0.6-2): the category value alone is not personal (closed structural enum, no free text, not a link, nullable and nulled by erasure); the health detail stays in the sealed absence facet. Evidence: without a clear column a reserve read would decrypt about 5,900 code lines a day to keep about 170. Every other table with a data subject stays envelope-only.","P32; ruling 