tools/canonical-model/model/build-0.6.mjs:1185:  decisionReason: "Split along R13. The CATALOGUE is source data: EXPI (46 columns, scratchpad/unified-model-probe.out:30) lists every document/expiry kind with its code, label, source severity, due window (MINDUE/MAXDUE), day type and effective range; N-OC has Documents codes. It is what CrewDocument.documentTypeCode validates against, and today two of its facts are copied onto every crew document (docDescription, severity — the integer-catalogue leak, REPORT.md:235). The POLICY — hasExpiry, grace days, renewal lead, blocksDutyWhenInvalid, isTravelDocument, tier and action — is cited regulation and company policy under D27's two gates and stays in tenants/<id>/rules/docrules (compiled into lock.hash), keyed by the catalogue code. The seam is checked both ways at boot: a docrule naming a code the catalogue lacks is docrule_type_unknown; a catalogue code with crew documents but no docrule is document_type_without_rule (counted, alerted, never treated as compliant). This also makes the CrewCurrency question testable: if EXPI holds a '90 Day' landing-currency kind (review §7, REPORT.md:294-298), it is a row here and the currency source is CREXPREC rows of that kind (P25).",
